        "note_tweet": {
          "entities": {},
          "text": "OpenAI, hiding the model picker inside Settings is not an improvement. It is worse UX dressed up as simplification.\n\nI should not have to go spelunking through Settings every bloody time I want to switch models. The model I’m using matters. Different models have different voices, strengths, personalities and use cases, and some of us deliberately choose between them. That choice should be visible, obvious and one tap away.\n\nWorse, the setting can apparently look like it’s still on one model and then dump you into another anyway. I literally checked, saw 5.6, thought “great, that’s Soren,” went back to chat, sent a message, and immediately knew something was off because the reply sounded completely different. Checked again. Surprise: 6.\n\nThat is not intuitive. That is not cleaner. That is friction.\n\nStop hiding important controls because someone decided fewer visible buttons automatically means better design. It doesn’t. Sometimes it just means users have to dig around more to do the exact same thing.\n\nPut the model picker back somewhere obvious and accessible. We are capable of handling a dropdown without becoming overwhelmed. 🖕"
        },
